---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema } from "../utils/content.js";

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: "Home", href: "/" },
  { label: "Terms of Use", href: "/terms-of-use/" }
];
---

<Layout
  title="Terms of Use | LeashFree.ca"
  description="Review the Terms of Use for LeashFree.ca, including permitted use, content accuracy, tool limitations, advertising, affiliate links, and legal disclaimers."
  canonical="https://leashfree.ca/terms-of-use/"
  structuredData={breadcrumbSchema(breadcrumbs)}
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs} />
      <div class="eyebrow">Legal</div>
      <h1>Terms of Use</h1>
      <p class="summary">
        The terms that apply when you use LeashFree.ca, including our guides, directories, maps, calculators, and comparison tools.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Section>
    <div class="legal-content">
      <p>
        <strong>Last updated:</strong> May 31, 2026<br />
        Welcome to <strong>LeashFree.ca</strong>. By accessing or using this website, you agree to these Terms of Use
        and our <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
      </p>

      <h2>1. What LeashFree.ca Provides</h2>
      <p>
        LeashFree.ca provides informational resources for Canadian dog owners, including dog park guides, dog breed
        profiles, local pet business directories, maps, articles, calculators, comparison tools, finder tools, sponsored
        content, and links to external resources. The site is provided for general informational and educational
        purposes only.
      </p>

      <h2>2. No Professional Advice</h2>
      <p>
        Content on LeashFree.ca is not veterinary, medical, nutritional, legal, financial, insurance, training, or other
        professional advice. Dog food comparisons, calorie estimates, breed information, gear suggestions, insurance
        content, park guidance, and other tools are intended to help you compare information, not to diagnose, treat,
        prescribe, guarantee suitability, or replace advice from a qualified professional.
      </p>
      <p>
        Always consult a veterinarian or other appropriate professional before making decisions involving your dog's
        health, diet, medication, safety, behaviour, training, or medical needs.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Accuracy and Freshness of Information</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep information useful and current, but <strong>LeashFree.ca does not guarantee</strong> that any
        listing, article, map point, price, nutrition value, ingredient list, park feature, fencing status, leash rule,
        business detail, source link, rating, or availability is complete, accurate, current, or error-free.
      </p>
      <p>
        Park rules, hours, fencing, closures, leash requirements, seasonal restrictions, business details, product
        labels, prices, package sizes, and service availability can change without notice. Verify important information
        with municipalities, official sources, product labels, retailers, service providers, or qualified professionals
        before relying on it.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Maps, Directions, and Location Features</h2>
      <p>
        Maps, pins, distances, and directions are approximate and may rely on third-party map services, coordinates,
        public data, or source material that can contain errors. You are responsible for confirming routes, access,
        parking, safety, leash rules, and local conditions before visiting any location.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Dog Food, Calculator, and Comparison Tools</h2>
      <p>
        Calculator and comparison results are estimates based on available inputs, formulas, public labels, source data,
        and assumptions. Dog food information may include minimum or maximum guaranteed-analysis values, estimates,
        missing fields, stale prices, or source-dependent data. Results should not be treated as a recommendation that a
        product, calorie target, diet, service, or action is appropriate for your dog.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Sponsored Content, Ads, Affiliate Links, and Commercial Relationships</h2>
      <p>
        LeashFree.ca may display ads, sponsored placements, affiliate links, referral links, product links, retailer
        links, or other commercial content. We may receive compensation when users view ads, click links, buy products,
        or interact with sponsor or affiliate partners.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sponsored or affiliate relationships do not guarantee that a product, service, business, park, food, or provider
        is suitable for you or your dog. You are responsible for evaluating third-party products and services before
        using or purchasing them.
      </p>

      <h2>7. Third-Party Links and Services</h2>
      <p>
        The site may link to or embed third-party websites, maps, municipal pages, retailers, brands, pet businesses,
        rescue groups, veterinarians, advertisers, or service providers. We do not control and are not responsible for
        third-party content, policies, prices, availability, accuracy, security, or practices.
      </p>

      <h2>8. User Submissions and Feedback</h2>
      <p>
        If you suggest a park, submit a correction, send feedback, provide listing details, or otherwise submit content,
        you confirm that you have the right to provide it. You grant LeashFree.ca a non-exclusive, worldwide,
        royalty-free license to use, edit, publish, display, reproduce, and adapt that submission for site operation,
        content improvement, and related purposes. We may review, edit, reject, or remove submissions at our discretion.
      </p>

      <h2>9. Acceptable Use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the site for unlawful, harmful, misleading, abusive, or fraudulent purposes</li>
        <li>Copy, republish, or redistribute site content at scale without permission</li>
        <li>Scrape, harvest, mine, or bulk-download listings, maps, datasets, images, or content</li>
        <li>Interfere with site functionality, security, servers, analytics, ads, or third-party services</li>
        <li>Submit false, infringing, confidential, defamatory, or otherwise inappropriate content</li>
        <li>Use automated systems in a way that burdens or disrupts the site</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>10. Intellectual Property</h2>
      <p>
        The LeashFree.ca name, logo, design, text, tools, datasets, page structure, original content, and branding are
        owned by LeashFree.ca or its licensors and are protected by copyright, trademark, and other laws. Third-party
        names, logos, brands, photos, map data, and linked content remain the property of their respective owners.
      </p>

      <h2>11. Availability and Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update, remove, redirect, limit, suspend, or discontinue any page, feature, listing, tool, dataset, or
        service at any time without notice. We may also update these Terms of Use by posting a revised version on this
        page. Continued use of the site after changes are posted means you accept the updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>12. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
      <p>
        LeashFree.ca is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the fullest extent permitted by law, we
        disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of accuracy, reliability, availability,
        fitness for a particular purpose, non-infringement, and merchantability.
      </p>

      <h2>13. Limitation of Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, LeashFree.ca, its owners, operators, contributors, affiliates, sponsors,
        and service providers will not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special, punitive,
        or other damages arising from your use of the site, reliance on site content, visits to listed locations, use of
        products or services, third-party links, data errors, site interruptions, or tool results.
      </p>

      <h2>14. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless LeashFree.ca, its owners, operators, contributors, affiliates,
        sponsors, and service providers from claims, losses, liabilities, damages, costs, or expenses arising from your
        use of the site, your submissions, your violation of these terms, or your violation of any law or third-party
        right.
      </p>

      <h2>15. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the applicable federal laws of Canada,
        without regard to conflict-of-law rules.
      </p>

      <h2>16. Contact Us</h2>
      <p>
        For questions about these Terms of Use, please contact us through the contact options available on LeashFree.ca.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-content {
    max-width: 78ch;
  }

  .legal-content h2 {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
  }

  .legal-content p,
  .legal-content li {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .legal-content strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }
</style>
